# Documentation rule — Next Connector

When you add or change **implemented** features in this project, update **both** files below. Document **only what exists in the codebase today** — no planned or future features.

## Files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `About_App_Readme.md` | Feature list and high-level summary of what the app does **so far** |
| `Learn.md` | Beginner-friendly deep guide: files, functions, variables, flows, and scenarios |

## When to update

- New route, webhook, worker, Prisma model, or npm script → update both files
- Behavior change to existing feature → update both files
- Removed feature → remove from both files

## When NOT to update

- Ideas, todos, or plan-only items not yet coded
- Duplicate content from `README.md` (Shopify template) unless relevant to our connector

## Style

- **About_App_Readme.md**: concise, feature-oriented, merchant/developer overview
- **Learn.md**: explain like teaching a beginner — stories, step-by-step flows, file → function → database paths

## Worker commands (reference)

Document any new worker in both files with its `npm run worker:*` command.
